; ============================================================
; TITLE:    My First Scale
; CATEGORY: Music & Sound
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     tone, scale, staircase, repeat
; SUMMARY:  Plays the C major scale up and down with TONE while the turtle climbs a staircase of colored steps.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The turtle builds a staircase, one colored step for each note of
;   the C major scale: do re mi fa sol la ti do. Each step plays its
;   note as it is drawn. Then the scale comes back down, and the
;   turtle walks down the stairs it built.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and turn your sound on. Change the number in
;   "make "beat 300" to play faster or slower.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * TONE plays one note: a frequency in hertz and a length in milliseconds
;   * a list can hold the numbers of a scale so a loop can walk through it
;   * FOREACH runs the same instructions for every item of a list
;   * higher frequency means higher pitch
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make the beat 150 for a fast scale, or 600 for a slow one.
;   * Swap the list for [262 294 330 392 440 523], a five-note scale
;     that sounds a little like a folk tune.
;   * Make the steps taller so the staircase fills the screen.
; ============================================================

; The frequencies of the C major scale, from middle C up to the next C.
; Each number is how many times per second the air shakes.
make "scale [262 294 330 349 392 440 494 523]

; How long each note lasts, in milliseconds (1000 is one second).
make "beat 300

; Colors for the eight steps, one for each note.
make "colors [4 14 6 2 3 1 13 5]

; Draw one step as a filled box, then move to the top right corner of
; it, ready for the next step.
to stair :c
  filled :c [repeat 2 [fd 30 rt 90 fd 60 rt 90]]
  fd 30 rt 90 fd 60 lt 90
end

to climb
  foreach :scale [
    stair item # :colors
    tone ? :beat
  ]
end

; Going down, we play the list backwards. The turtle steps down too,
; without drawing, so you can follow it with your eyes.
to descend
  penup
  foreach reverse :scale [
    tone ? :beat
    lt 90 fd 60 rt 90 bk 30
  ]
  pendown
end

clearscreen
setbackground [250 245 230]
penup setxy -240 -150 pendown
climb
wait 30
descend
penup setxy -110 160 pendown
setpencolor 0
label [do re mi fa sol la ti do]
hideturtle
